      "writtenOn": "2020-03-11T17:49:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"dependency\", for clarity?\n\nFor example, in the ART module libdexfile_external will be an external member listed in native_shared_libs. It depends on libdexfile (among others) which is in the ART module but not part of the SDK. I take it that libdexfile is an internal member?\n\nIf so, I understand from the below that libdexfile will also get a cc_prebuilt_library module in the snapshot, just for the sake of the dependency tracking (otherwise it wouldn\u0027t be known to Soong in the prefixed and suffixed form).\n\nIf that\u0027s correct, then why not instead transitively collect the external dependencies of the internal members and add them to the exported members?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 196,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 196,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "71b5701d259219953a128658df63227e67f8180e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8bd050a5_5d11fb9c",
        "filename": "android/sdk.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 196,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-11T18:15:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As mentioned in another comment there are no internal cc members yet.\n\nIf libdexfile_external depends on libdexfile then if the libdexfile should not be depended on by other parties then libdexfile_external should be stubs and in the sdk and libdexfile should only be in the apex not in the sdk.\n\nIf libdexfile_external is needed on the host then we would also need to add libdexfile to the host to make that work.\n\n\"If that\u0027s correct, then why not instead transitively collect the external dependencies of the internal members and add them to the exported members?\"\n\nAFAIK there is no distinction made between external/internal dependencies of a library. e.g. there is nothing in libdexfile_external (except the name which we cannot rely on) that distinguishes it from libdexfile and nothing in that which distinguishes it from say liblog. So, we could not tell which ones to include internally and which ones not to include.\n\nAlso, we need to make sure that we do not accidentally include libraries that belong in other sdks.\n\nLonger term I expect each sdk/module_exports to reference the other sdks/module_exports that it relies upon so that we can differentiate between internal / external members better. That is going to be difficult though as there are cycles between them that would need to be broken, e.g. conscrypt sdk -\u003e art sdk -\u003e conscrypt sdk",
      "parentUuid": "b939441c_6f8d4cfb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 196,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 196,
        "endChar": 23
      },
